    "body": "Hm... I guess we can just do `element.matches(':disabled')` too but I guess that's clunky. Maybe `getDisabledState()`?\r\n\r\nI don't like \"computed\" prefix or suffix because that's awfully luminescent of computed style / value of CSS, and overloading the term \"computed\" for other purposes is rather confusing.",
